<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marengo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-second-coalition">War of the Second Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marengo was fought on 14 June 1800 near Alessandria in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> between the French army of the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> and an Austrian army under General Michael von Melas. Close to defeat in the afternoon, the French won after the arrival of General Desaix's division; Desaix was killed in the counter-attack. The victory restored French control of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and strengthened Napoleon's position in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marengo.jpg" alt="Battle of Marengo" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis-François, Baron Lejeune · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lejeune_-_Bataille_de_Marengo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
